# 28. My recommended priority order

Because **you're the only developer**, I would not spend two weeks establishing architecture before delivering the first feature.

I'd approach it in this order:

### Phase 1 — Foundation

Get these right:

```text
Angular project
TypeScript strictness
Standalone architecture
Routing
Figma design tokens
Material 3 theme
ESLint
Formatting
Git
Azure Pipeline
```

### Phase 2 — First real feature

Build one complete feature end-to-end:

```text
Figma
  ↓
Component
  ↓
Service
  ↓
API
  ↓
Error handling
  ↓
Loading states
  ↓
Tests
  ↓
CI/CD
```

This is important because you'll discover architectural problems by actually building something.

### Phase 3 — Stabilize the patterns

Once you've built the first feature, extract the patterns that genuinely repeat:

```text
API handling
Forms
Loading
Errors
Dialogs
Tables
Notifications
Permissions
```

Then turn those patterns into reusable infrastructure.

### Phase 4 — Scale cautiously

Only after you've encountered real complexity should you consider:

```text
More sophisticated state management
Nx
Angular libraries
advanced caching
custom tooling
micro-frontends
```

